<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Duiker year shr jumps, hikes dividend.</title>
<headline>Duiker year shr jumps, hikes dividend.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     103.5	 vs 63.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 47.0	  vs 25.0</p>
<p>    Mining income	   259.48	vs 142.99</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   245.01	vs 138.87</p>
<p>    Tax			 80.71	 vs 47.29</p>
<p>    Interest income	 14.68	 vs 10.77</p>
<p>    Turnover		1,043.68	vs 664.05</p>
<p>Div payable November 27</p>
<p>on register November 15</p>
<p>Full name: Duiker Mining Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - South African coal and gold miner Duiker said its mining revenue had increased because of higher prices realised, a weaker exchange rate and higher sales volumes of bituminous coal, anthracite and gold.</p>
<p>The firm said its Klipwal Gold Mine saw its average gold price rise from 44,615 rand a kilogramme to 51,600 rand/kg. Its average cost of production improved from 55,265 rand/kg to 38,364 rand/kg.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
